course: dictionary
lesson: 4122
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Glass can be a hard clear material for windows, a cup for drinking, or the glasses people wear on their faces. Read the words around it to find out which one the writer means. «A glass of water» is a cup and the amount it holds, not a window.
explain: «A boy in Halifax squints at the board and sits closer and closer; his teacher notices, he has an eye test, and with new glasses the letters are sharp again.» Squinting and sitting closer tell you the boy cannot see well. New glasses here are the things he wears on his face to help him see.
explain: «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant and the bent light makes the ant look huge.» Here glass means a lens, a piece of glass that bends light. Being careful matters: the same lens can gather sunlight into a tiny burning spot, so never point it at the Sun or at anything alive.
fact: Glass is a hard, clear material that you can see through. It is used for windows, bottles and jars.
fact: A glass is a cup made of glass for drinking. A glass of juice means the amount the cup holds.
fact: Glasses are a pair of lenses in a frame that people wear to see better. You use the plural glasses for them.
fact: Glass breaks easily. Broken glass can cut you, so tell an adult and do not pick it up with your hands.
fact: «Glass» is made from sand heated very hot, and it lets light through.
exercise: The teacher says, «Pass me a glass of water, please.» What does glass mean here? | A pair of glasses | *A cup for drinking | A window | A hard material for jars only
exercise: «With new glasses the letters are sharp again.» What are the glasses? | *Two lenses in a frame that you wear to see better | A bottle of juice | A cup for drinking | A window in a classroom
exercise: What is glass made from, according to the science lesson? | *Sand heated very hot | Iron mixed with water | Wood cut into thin sheets | Plastic melted in the sun
test: «A shiny glaze, which is a thin coat of glass, makes a mug waterproof.» What makes the mug waterproof? | A thick coat of paint | *A thin coat of glass | Hot sand | A wooden lid
test: In «a glass of water», what does glass mean? | A pair of glasses | A window | A hard material you can see through, like a window | *A cup, and the amount it holds
exam: You find broken glass on the classroom floor. What should you do? | Pick it up quickly with your hands | Sweep it up with your feet | *Tell an adult and do not touch it | Throw it in the bin with your bare hands
